  "term": "corticotropin-releasing factor",
  "definition": "Corticotropin-releasing factor is a small peptide hormone that promotes release of adrenocorticotropic hormone from the pituitary. It is mainly produced by hypothalamic neurons and is also made in some other tissues, including the placenta, adrenal medulla, and testis.",
